      "message": "Not sure exactly what you meant here, but I\u0027m going to try respond based on what I think you meant.\n\nGetRenderCaps() is exactly identical to GetDeviceCaps(FXDC_RENDER_CAPS) as of now, no behavioural changes should be there, just purely a rename. In the next CL the plan would be to change GetRenderCaps() as a whole to booleans/masks.\n\nThe reason for GetRenderCaps() rather than having it a part of GetDeviceCaps() were a few things as we end up in one of 2 possibilities.\n\n1. We end up passing an int to GetDeviceCaps() and then have only one case which makes the work look half-done.\n\n2. We end up with a GetDeviceCaps() that calls all these individual functions and has to be replaced in CL2 leading to CL2 being very large.\n\nTL;DR: None of the Render Caps behaviour changed here, just renamed GetDeviceCaps(FXDC_RENDER_CAPS) to GetRenderCaps() here.\n\nIf you want me to revert this let me know, but I feel reverting this could cause more problems later on. Let me know if I missed something here. Thanks!",
